  "editorial_md": "### Intuition\nBuild the string one character at a time and never let it become unbalanced. A `(` is allowed while fewer than `n` have been used; a `)` is allowed only while it would close an open `(`.\n\n### Algorithm\n```python\ndef generateParenthesis(n):\n    out = []\n\n    def build(prefix, opened, closed):\n        if len(prefix) == 2 * n:\n            out.append(prefix)\n            return\n        if opened < n:\n            build(prefix + '(', opened + 1, closed)\n        if closed < opened:\n            build(prefix + ')', opened, closed + 1)\n\n    build('', 0, 0)\n    return out\n```\n\nBecause invalid prefixes are never extended, every string that reaches length `2n` is valid, and no work is wasted on dead ends.\n\n### Complexity\nProportional to the number of answers (the n-th Catalan number) times `n`.",
